<title>UK: Ship carrying titanium slag aground in St Lawrence.</title>
<headline>Ship carrying titanium slag aground in St Lawrence.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The bulk carrier Utviken, carrying a cargo of titanium slag, ran aground in the St. Lawrence Seaway upstream from Valleyfield, Quebec, on Tuesday, Lloyd's Shipping Intelligence Service said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The 30,052-dwt ship is still hard aground with damage to its port side forward/amidships, Lloyd's said. Its forepeak and no.1 double bottom tank are flooded, though all other tanks are dry.</p>
<p>The Bahamas-registered ship was en route from Richards Bay, South Africa, to Detroit.</p>
